# moby-gstage.manifest - freecam poses for the moby vertex stage readback
# (tests/harness/check_moby_gstage_ab.sh, tools/moby_gstage_ab.py).
#
# One row per pose:  <level>[@variant] | pos=(x, y, z) yaw=Y pitch=P | [start VBL] | [LOD tiers]
#   level  a --skip-to-level name
#   pose   a freecam pose string (the per-tick freecam log format, verbatim)
#   start  the capture VBL (default: the freecam corpus's canonical VBL)
#   tiers  the --lod values captured (default: the harness's --lods)
# and carve-out rows:  carve-out | <class> | <reason>
#
# The freecam corpus's first Dark Hollow row. (The second Artisans row is not
# used: its presented scene carries no moby identity of a record pass, so
# the readback cannot be paired with it.)
dark_hollow | pos=(86434, 27639, 17265) yaw=3048 pitch=243
# Recordings (games/spyro-1/bk2), at a pinned VBL of the presentation corpus:
# moving and animated mobys, the sub-tick pose lerp, mobys near the camera.
bk2:artisans-balloonist | | 3130
bk2:cliff-town-vista | | 1783
bk2:level-transition-gems | | 2440
# The shaded pass (moby.c shaded_project_moby; the shaded, billboard and
# drawscale classes): a gem close to the camera, its metal faces in the near
# band; the portal-name text glyphs, which take the tie pull; gems spilling
# from a broken chest. level-transition-gems above draws the tally gems as
# billboards.
bk2:stone-hill-gem-spyro-occlusion | | 1896
bk2:beast-makers-wild-flight-text | | 3310
bk2:chest-destruction | | 2332
# The Gnasty fight's blast dome: records with a GPF byte (the GPF class).
bk2:gnasty_gnorc_attack | | 1796
bk2:gnasty_gnorc_attack@1808 | | 1808
#
carve-out | mirrored | no freecam row draws a record whose rotation has a negative determinant; a mirror-twin row is owed
carve-out | shell | Spyro 1 lists no sphere-shell class (game_layout.moby.sphere_shell_n is 0)
carve-out | drawscale | no row draws a shaded moby with a nonzero m_ScaleOverride (every shaded record of the rows above has W factor 2); a row is owed
carve-out | simple | Spyro 1 draws its simple models through the shaded pass (moby_game.simple_pass is NULL)
carve-out | simplescreen | Spyro 1 draws its simple models through the shaded pass (moby_game.simple_pass is NULL)
